Translation patch: libsignal_protocol::triple_ratchet (five error messages)

Change: the literals "version does not fit in u8", "encrypt", "decrypt", "invalid sender chain message keys" and "invalid receiver chain message keys" move to the constants `VERSION_DOES_NOT_FIT_IN_U8`, `ENCRYPT_OPERATION`, `DECRYPT_OPERATION`, `INVALID_SENDER_CHAIN_MESSAGE_KEYS` and `INVALID_RECEIVER_CHAIN_MESSAGE_KEYS`, with the same bytes.
Why: Aeneas loses a string literal returned from a closure or an early return ("There should be no bottoms in the value"; blocker catalog NO-BOTTOMS).
Behaviour: identical.
Applies after: protocol-triple_ratchet-address_pair.patch, protocol-triple_ratchet-decrypt-aes_cbc_errors.patch, protocol-triple_ratchet-decrypt-spqr_errors.patch (their lines are this patch's context).

